  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Jackson Merrill broke the game open with two home runs, but this was decided long before Song's ninth-inning double.",
    "what_this_means": "Merrill's power defined the early offense. He was responsible for nearly half their runs through six innings. But the real story was the game's shape. Down one after the first inning, they led by four after the second and never looked back. By the time Song sparked the ninth-inning rally, the result was already settled. The lineup got runners in scoring position 24 times and converted 10 of those at-bats into runs. That's not a collapse in clutch situations. That's execution when it mattered, even if it came against a team that didn't fight back. Matsui and V\u00e1squez combined for six scoreless innings of relief. The bullpen held while the bats finished what they started early. This team doesn't need drama to win. Sometimes they just build a lead and keep it.",
